---
source: crates/mori-checker/src/tests.rs
description: "Code:\n\nprofile \"moriarty-beta/1\";\nagreement Values {\n  domain Preview = { id: \"preview\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"preview\" };\n  asset USD = { domain: Preview, id: \"usd\", scale: 2, representation: \"native\" };\n  const tip = 5;\n  const total = 10 + 5 USD;\n  const other = 5 USD - tip;\n}\n"
---
mori::check::number_and_amount

  × I cannot add a plain number and a `USD` amount.
   ╭─[test.mori:6:22]
 5 │   const tip = 5;
 6 │   const total = 10 + 5 USD;
   ·                 ─┬   ──┬──
   ·                  │     ╰── this is a `USD` amount
   ·                  ╰── this is a plain number
 7 │   const other = 5 USD - tip;
   ╰────
  help: Give the number its asset, so both sides are `USD` amounts:

            const total = 10 USD + 5 USD;

mori::check::number_and_amount

  × I cannot subtract a plain number from a `USD` amount.
   ╭─[test.mori:7:25]
 6 │   const total = 10 + 5 USD;
 7 │   const other = 5 USD - tip;
   ·                 ──┬──   ─┬─
   ·                   │      ╰── this is a plain number
   ·                   ╰── this is a `USD` amount
 8 │ }
   ╰────
  help: A plain number and an amount cannot be combined. Use amounts of the
        same asset on both sides.
